<title>INDIA: India says 96/97 trade gap at around $5.0 billion.</title>
<headline>India says 96/97 trade gap at around $5.0 billion.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's trade deficit in fiscal 1996/97(April-March) is likely to be around $5.0 billion, a senior Commerce Ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;It will be around $5.0 billion,&quot; P.P. Prabhu, the highest ranking civil servant in the Commerce Ministry, told reporters when asked about the likely deficit in the fiscal year which ends today.</p>
</text>
